(cont'd) ## Methodology
Since Prokudin-Gorskii used a special camera that exposed the same scene three times in quick succession through red, green and blue filters, each exposure was recorded on a different part of the glass plate, often stacked vertically. The structure of each image is therefore a single grayscale plate divided into three equal vertical sections (B, G, R). Because the three filtered exposures were captured one after another and stored as stacked sections on a single plate, they don’t line up automatically. To reconstruct a sharp color photo, we must first split the plate into its three channels and then align them; otherwise, the final image will show strong color fringes and blurring:


```tikz
\begin{document}
\begin{tikzpicture}[line width=1pt]

% --- Left: vertical B/G/R strip ---
\draw[blue, fill=blue, fill opacity=0.1]  (0,  3) rectangle (2, 2); \node at (1, 2.5) {\bfseries B};
\draw[green, fill=green, fill opacity=0.1] (0, 1.95) rectangle (2, 1); \node at (1, 1.5) {\bfseries G};
\draw[red, fill=red, fill opacity=0.1]   (0, 0.95) rectangle (2, 0); \node at (1, 0.5) {\bfseries R};

% Arrow to middle
\draw[->] (3, 1.5) -- (4, 1.5);
\node[align=center] at (3.5, 0.8) {Split \\ Channels};

% --- Middle: fanned stack (alignment) ---
\begin{scope}[shift={(5.0,0)}]
  \draw[blue, fill=blue, fill opacity=0.33]  (0,0) rectangle (2,2);
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(5.5,0.5)}]
  \draw[green, fill=green, fill opacity=0.33] (0,0) rectangle (2,2);
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(6,1)}]
  \draw[red, fill=red, fill opacity=0.33]   (0,0) rectangle (2,2);
\end{scope}

% Arrow to right
\draw[->] (9, 1.5) -- (10, 1.5);
\node at (9.5, 1) {Alignment};

% --- Right: "Colored Image" with simple multi-color border ---
\begin{scope}[shift={(11,0)}]
  \draw[blue,  line width=3pt] (0,0) rectangle (3,3);
  \draw[green, line width=2pt] (0.15,0.15) rectangle (2.85,2.85);
  \draw[red,   line width=1pt] (0.30,0.30) rectangle (2.70,2.70);
  \node[align=center] at (1.5,1.5) {Colored \\ Image};
\end{scope}

\end{tikzpicture}
