>[!note] Stability in Continuous-Time LTI Difference Equation Model w/ No Input
>For an **input-less** [[99c Continuous-Time LTI Models|continuous-time LTI model]] $\frac{d}{dt}\vec{x}(t)=A\vec{x}(t)$ with $\vec{x}(0)=\vec{x}_0$, where $A \in \mathbb{R}^{n \times n}$ has eigenvalues $\lambda_1,...,\lambda_n$, the model is:
